# SPA routes — rewrite to the app shell with a 200 status.
# Keep the rule set free of `?param` clauses: wisp's _redirects matcher
# compares the rule LHS against path + query, so a rule without an
# explicit query spec silently fails to match URLs that carry one.
# (See CLAUDE.md, "Hosting: wisp.place".)  Multiplayer uses a # hash
# fragment for its DID list precisely because hashes never reach wisp.
/              /index.html   200
/multiplayer/:tid   /index.html   200
/:actor        /index.html   200
/:actor/:tid   /index.html   200

# Anything else is not a real page — serve the app shell with a 404 status.
/*             /index.html   404
